{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Litv5ARWqh4GG7e8BiZNLE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\texperiments:\n2\t  # === Claim 1: Classification vs Generation ===\n3\t  - id: cwm-baseline\n4\t    claim: 1\n5\t    description: \"Train CWM generation baseline (Qwen3-4B LoRA, same data/config as MVP-B) to predict execution output instead of pass/fail. Compare per-class F1 against classification model (87.1/87.9%).\"\n6\t    priority: P0\n7\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n8\t    deps: [mvp-b-train]\n9\t    status: PREPARING\n10\t    registry_id: cwm-baseline\n11\t\n12\t  - id: multi-seed-core\n13\t    claim: 1\n14\t    description: \"Multi-seed validation for core comparison: run classification (mvp-b-train) and CWM baseline each with seeds {0, 1, 42}. Report mean +/- std F1. Statistical significance via paired t-test or bootstrap CI. Required for any claim of 'significantly better'.\"\n15\t    priority: P0\n16\t    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n17\t    deps: [cwm-baseline]\n18\t\n19\t  - id: trace-then-judge\n20\t    claim: 1\n21\t    description: \"Trace-then-Judge ablation (chain-of-thought, NOT pipeline): single Qwen3-4B model trained to first generate a brief execution reasoning trace (~50 tokens describing expected behavior), then output pass/fail. Same LoRA config/data. Tests whether explicit execution reasoning helps or hurts compared to direct classification. If trace-then-judge >= direct classification, the advantage is from task simplicity, not from skipping reasoning.\"\n22\t    priority: P0\n23\t    gpu_budget_hours: 4\n24\t    deps: [cwm-baseline]\n25\t\n26\t  - id: traj-level-finetuned\n27\t    claim: 1\n28\t    description: \"Same-size fine-tuned trajectory-level baseline: Qwen3-4B LoRA trained to predict resolved/unresolved. Data construction: for each problem_id, aggregate all (code, test) pairs into (code, all_tests_concatenated) -> resolved (original code passes all tests) / unresolved (mutated code fails any test). Same train/val/test split by problem_id. Isolates granularity effect.\"\n29\t    priority: P0\n30\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n31\t    deps: [mvp-b-data-prep]\n32\t\n33\t  - id: model-size-scaling\n34\t    claim: 1\n35\t    description: \"Scale classification model from 4B to 8B. Measure accuracy improvement and compare with CWM at 8B. Determine if classification advantage holds across scales.\"\n36\t    priority: P1\n37\t    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n38\t    deps: [cwm-baseline]\n39\t\n40\t  # === Claim 2: Diagnostic Signals ===\n41\t  - id: diagnostic-rerepair\n42\t    claim: 2\n43\t    description: \"Downstream proof-of-concept: give repair agent per-test failure predictions vs no per-test info, compare resolve rate on 200 instances. Uses SWE-agent or similar repair framework.\"\n44\t    priority: P1\n45\t    gpu_budget_hours: 12\n46\t    deps: [cwm-baseline, traj-level-finetuned]\n47\t\n48\t  - id: per-test-precision-recall\n49\t    claim: 2\n50\t    description: \"Measure per-test failure prediction precision/recall against ground-truth failing tests on full test set. Evaluate diagnostic signal quality without downstream execution.\"\n51\t    priority: P0\n52\t    gpu_budget_hours: 1\n53\t    deps: [mvp-b-train]\n54\t\n55\t  # === Claim 3: Accuracy-Utility Frontier ===\n56\t  - id: oracle-f2p-stratified\n57\t    claim: 3\n58\t    description: \"Stratified oracle analysis by F2P test count (T=1, T=2, T=3+). Report per-test advantage breakdown showing advantage concentrates in multi-test instances.\"\n59\t    priority: P0\n60\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n61\t    deps: [mvp-a-oracle-sim]\n62\t\n63\t  - id: oracle-total-validated\n64\t    claim: 3\n65\t    description: \"Oracle study with Total (F2P+P2P) distribution at empirically measured regression rates. Validate when P2P tests help vs hurt.\"\n66\t    priority: P0\n67\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n68\t    deps: [p2p-regression-rate]\n69\t    status: DONE\n70\t    registry_id: mvp-a-oracle-sim\n71\t\n72\t  - id: block-corr-empirical\n73\t    claim: 3\n74\t    description: \"Empirically validate block-correlation assumption: measure actual prediction error correlation structure from trained model's test-level predictions, compare with i.i.d. and block-correlated simulation models.\"\n75\t    priority: P2\n76\t    gpu_budget_hours: 1\n77\t    deps: [mvp-b-train]\n78\t\n79\t  # === Repo-level Extension (if resources allow) ===\n80\t  - id: swebench-pertest-data\n81\t    claim: [1, 2, 3]\n82\t    description: \"Docker re-evaluation of SWE-bench Verified patches to extract per-test labels. Build SWE-bench-PerTest dataset (500 instances x 16 candidates). Resource contribution.\"\n83\t    priority: P1\n84\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n85\t    compute_note: \"CPU/Docker only, ~16-24h with 16 parallel containers. Start early to parallelize with GPU experiments.\"\n86\t    deps: []\n87\t\n88\t  - id: repo-level-training\n89\t    claim: [1, 2]\n90\t    description: \"Fine-tune Qwen3-4B/8B on repo-level (patched_code, test_code) -> pass/fail using SWE-bench-PerTest data. Evaluate on held-out instances.\"\n91\t    priority: P1\n92\t    gpu_budget_hours: 12\n93\t    deps: [swebench-pertest-data]\n94\t\n95\t  # === Baselines (Part 3 Pareto comparison) ===\n96\t  - id: llm-judge-baseline\n97\t    claim: [1, 3]\n98\t    description: \"Qwen3-8B/32B zero-shot LLM-as-judge baselines (trajectory-level and per-test). Reference points for Pareto frontier.\"\n99\t    priority: P1\n100\t    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n101\t    deps: []\n102\t\n103\t  - id: per-test-majority-voting\n104\t    claim: 1\n105\t    description: \"Per-test majority voting (K=3) with classification model. Test if self-consistency improves per-test accuracy.\"\n106\t    priority: P2\n107\t    gpu_budget_hours: 3\n108\t    deps: [mvp-b-train]\n109\t\n110\t# Kill condition (D005): CWM baseline comparison must show >=3pp F1 difference\n111\t# with p<0.05 across 3 seeds. If not met, consider kill.\n112\t\n113\t# GPU Budget Summary (updated):\n114\t# P0 total: ~17h (cwm 2h + multi-seed 8h + trace-then-judge 4h + traj-level 2h + per-test-pr 1h + oracle 0h)\n115\t# P1 total: ~40h (model-scaling 8h + diagnostic 12h + swebench-data 0h + repo-training 12h + llm-judge 8h)\n116\t# P2 total: ~4h (block-corr 1h + majority-voting 3h)\n117\t# Grand total: ~61h on RTX 5090 (available: ~336h over 14 days, well within budget)\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e2ff9bf-0df6-4a54-a6c1-9e43e44e7de7","uuid":"692fd4b3-364c-4666-8fef-7f6528620d41","timestamp":"2026-05-11T21:54:12.637Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/experiment_plan.yaml","content":"experiments:\n  # === Claim 1: Classification vs Generation ===\n  - id: cwm-baseline\n    claim: 1\n    description: \"Train CWM generation baseline (Qwen3-4B LoRA, same data/config as MVP-B) to predict execution output instead of pass/fail. Compare per-class F1 against classification model (87.1/87.9%).\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n    deps: [mvp-b-train]\n    status: PREPARING\n    registry_id: cwm-baseline\n\n  - id: multi-seed-core\n    claim: 1\n    description: \"Multi-seed validation for core comparison: run classification (mvp-b-train) and CWM baseline each with seeds {0, 1, 42}. Report mean +/- std F1. Statistical significance via paired t-test or bootstrap CI. Required for any claim of 'significantly better'.\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n    deps: [cwm-baseline]\n\n  - id: trace-then-judge\n    claim: 1\n    description: \"Trace-then-Judge ablation (chain-of-thought, NOT pipeline): single Qwen3-4B model trained to first generate a brief execution reasoning trace (~50 tokens describing expected behavior), then output pass/fail. Same LoRA config/data. Tests whether explicit execution reasoning helps or hurts compared to direct classification. If trace-then-judge >= direct classification, the advantage is from task simplicity, not from sk