# with p<0.05 across 3 seeds. If not met, consider kill.\n\n# GPU Budget Summary (updated):\n# P0 total: ~17h (cwm 2h + multi-seed 8h + trace-then-judge 4h + traj-level 2h + per-test-pr 1h + oracle 0h)\n# P1 total: ~40h (model-scaling 8h + diagnostic 12h + swebench-data 0h + repo-training 12h + llm-judge 8h)\n# P2 total: ~4h (block-corr 1h + majority-voting 3h)\n# Grand total: ~61h on RTX 5090 (available: ~336h over 14 days, well within budget)\n","numLines":118,"startLine":1,"totalLines":118}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QHt2qezD4JY227fpzoNto3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a complete picture. Let me construct the detailed median-tier imagined experiments for all planned experiments. Let me go through each one:\n\n1. **cwm-baseline** (PREPARING) - CWM generation baseline\n2. **multi-seed-core** - Multi-seed validation  \n3. **trace-then-judge** - Trace-then-Judge ablation\n4. **traj-level-finetuned** - Trajectory-level fine-tuned baseline\n5. **model-size-scaling** - 4B→8B scaling\n\n\n6. **diagnostic-rerepair** - Downstream re-repair\n7. **per-test-precision-recall** - Per-test precision/recall\n8. **oracle-f2p-stratified** - Stratified oracle analysis\n9. **oracle-total-validated** (DONE) - Already completed\n10. **block-corr-empirical** - Block correlation empirical\n11. **swebench-pertest-data** - SWE-bench per-test data\n12. **repo-level-training** - Repo-level training\n13. **llm-judge-baseline** - LLM judge baseline\n14. **per-test** - Continuing with the remaining experiments\n\nFor each incomplete experiment, I need to generate median-tier predictions with supporting rationales. Looking at the median tier thresholds across different metrics—CWM generation F1 scores around 77-82%, classification gaps of 5-10%, trace-then-judge performance in the 79-84% range, and various other benchmarks—I can see the Classification MVP-B is already performing well at 87.1% pass F1 and 87.9% fail F1, which gives me a baseline to work from.\n\nThe narrative around these results needs some refinement: the accuracy-efficiency tradeoff claim requires more careful framing, the trace-then-judge findings are somewhat ambiguous and need clarification on what's confounding the results, and I should reframe the diagnostic signal quality as more suggestive than definitive. The strongest contribution appears to be in claim 3.\n\nFor the CWM baseline experiment, I'm predicting per-class F1 around 79-80% as the midpoint of the median range, which would create roughly a 7.5 percentage point gap from the 87.5% overall accuracy—well within the expected 5-10% range. The reasoning here is that CWM struggles with generating exact execution output strings, particularly for complex assertions, format mismatches, and floating point precision issues, even though it handles simpler cases like basic equality checks reasonably well.\n\nAt the 4B scale with LoRA fine-tuning, token budget constraints become a real bottleneck when dealing with complex outputs, so that 7-8 percentage point gap reflects CWM successfully handling roughly 70% of straightforward cases but failing on the remaining 30% where outputs are more intricate.\n\nFor the multi-seed experiment, I'm expecting classification-based seeds to cluster tightly around 86.8-87.4% F1 with minimal variance, while CWM seeds will show wider scatter between 78.5-80.5% F1. The gap should be around 7.2 percentage points with a standard deviation of about 1.3, statistically significant at p < 0.05. This makes sense because the classification task has a simpler output space that converges more reliably, whereas generation quality for CWM is more sensitive to random initialization—some seeds just happen to learn better output formatting patterns than others.\n\nFor trace-then-judge, I'm looking at an F1 score around 81% as the midpoint estimate.\n\nThe trace-then-judge approach sits in the middle ground—it captures some structured reasoning from the trace generation but introduces noise since the model sometimes generates incorrect traces and then either correctly or incorrectly extracts the final judgment from them. This creates a confounding effect where the 6-point gap between trace-then-judge and pure classification is smaller than the 8-point gap between classification and CWM, making it hard to tell whether the benefit comes from avoiding generation altogether or just from the task being simpler.\n\nFor trajectory-level fine-tuning, aggregating all tests into a single trajectory makes the prediction harder since the model needs to handle longer concatenated inputs and output just one resolved/unresolved label, so it ends up slightly easier than CWM but harder than per-test classification.\n\nWhen scaling from 4B to 8B parameters, both approaches improve but CWM benefits more because the extra capacity helps with output generation, yet the fundamental gap between generation and classification persists. The diagnostic re-repair experiment shows a modest 2.5% resolve rate lift that doesn't reach statistical significance at n=200, suggesting that per-test failure information provides some help but the effect is limited. repair agent focus on specific failing tests, but the improvement is modest because (a) many instances have T=1 where per-test = trajectory-level, (b) the per-test predictions have ~20% error rate which sometimes misguides the repair agent, and (c) n=200 is underpowered to detect a ~2.5% effect. This is why median tier frames it as \"pilot\" rather than main result.\n\nThe model's precision and recall on test predictions are both around 0.74–0.78, meaning it correctly identifies most failing tests but has a meaningful false positive rate—roughly 1 in 5 \"this test fails\" predictions is incorrect, which limits how much the downstream diagnostics can actually help.\n\nThe per-test advantage really only kicks in when there are multiple F2P tests; with T=1 (which covers 69% of SWE-bench), per-test and trajectory-level predictions are nearly equivalent, so the population-level benefit gets diluted. When T≥2, the gains climb to 8–25%, but that's a minority of instances.\n\nI'm also seeing a weak correlation of around 0.18 between block structure and the outcomes. Repo-level classification drops to around 74% F1 due to increased complexity from cross-file dependencies, more intricate test patterns, and a smaller training set compared to function-level work, though it still substantially outperforms the majority baseline. For LLM judges, zero-shot performance ranges from 62-72% depending on model size and evaluation approach, with larger models performing better but still lacking the fine-tuning signal needed for stronger results.\n\nMajority voting with K=3 yields only a modest 1 percentage point improvement to 88.5% F1, suggesting the classification task is already well-calibrated and the marginal gains don't justify the 3x computational cost.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2131,"cache_read_input_tokens":45680,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2131},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e2ff9bf-0df6-4a54-a6c1-9e43e44e7de7","uuid":"40b498d6-7433-423f-bf5c-4f1ca2d50469"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QHt2qezD4JY227fpzoNto3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the context needed. Let me produce the detailed median-tier imagined experiments.\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claim 1 降调: classification 在 4B 规模下有 5-10pp F1 优势，但不能说 \"fundamentally simpler\"，\n  改为 \"favorable accuracy-efficiency tradeoff at small model scales\"。Trace-then-Judge 落在\n  classification 和 CWM 之间，confound 无法干净分离——需要诚实讨论。\n  Claim 2 弱化: per-test precision/recall 尚可但非压倒性（~78%/74%），re-repair lift ~2.5% 在\n  n=200 下不显著，作为 pilot evidence 而非 main result。\n  Claim 3 成为论文最强贡献: oracle frontier 分析 + stratified T 分析 + block correlation 实测\n  提供清晰的 decision framework。\n  整体 reframe 为 \"When and Why Per-Test Simulation Helps\"，以 Claim 3 的 characterization 为主轴，\n  Claim 1 的 classification advantage 为支撑。EMNLP Findings 更稳妥，Main 需要 Claim 2 突破或\n  Claim 3 叙事特别精彩。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"CWM Generation Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"cwm-baseline\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B LoRA 训练预测执行输出（generation），同数据同配置对比 classification (87.1/87.9% F1)。\n    expected_results:\n      cwm_pass_f1: 0.79\n      cwm_fail_f1: 0.80\n      cwm_overall_accuracy: 0.795\n      cwm_per_class_f1_avg: 0.795\n      classification_minus_cwm_gap_pp: 7.8\n      cwm_token_budget_exhaust_rate: 0.12\n      cwm_string_mismatch_rate: 0.18\n    result_rationale: >\n      CWM 在简单 assertion 测试（assertEqual, assertTrue）上表现接近 classification，因为输出\n      短且可预测。但在复杂输出场景下显著退化：(1) ~12% 的样本因输出超过 LoRA 微调时的 max_new_tokens\n      而被截断，导致无法提取正确答案；(2) ~18% 的样本因字符串值预测错误（浮点精度、格式差异、\n      动态值如时间戳）而判错。这两个失败模式正是 Debugging CWMs 论文指出的核心问题。\n      4B 模型容量有限，无法同时学好\"理解代码语义\"和\"精确生成输出字符串\"，导致 per-class F1\n      落在 79-80%，比 classification 低约 8pp。这个 gap 处于 moderate 范围——足以支撑\n      \"classification 有优势\"的叙事，但不足以称为 \"fundamentally simpler\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Classification vs Generation (4B, Function-level)\"\n        columns: [Model, Formulation, Pass_F1, Fail_F1, Avg_F1, Accuracy]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-4B LoRA, Classification, 0.871, 0.879, 0.875, 0.875]\n          - [Qwen3-4B LoRA, \"CWM Generation\", 0.79, 0.80, 0.795, 0.795]\n          - [Delta, \"-\", \"+8.1pp\", \"+7.9pp\", \"+8.0pp\", \"+8.0pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Error analysis pie chart: CWM failure modes 分解 — token exhaustion 12%, string mismatch 18%, semantic error 70%\"\n    analysis: >\n      8pp gap 在 median 档是 make-or-break 的边界值。需要 multi-seed 验证确认 gap 稳定且显著。\n      如果 multi-seed 方差大到 CI 包含 3pp（kill 线），论文核心论点受威胁。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Core Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"multi-seed-core\"\n    description: >\n      Classification 和 CWM 各 3 个 seed {0, 1, 42}，报告 mean ± std，paired t-test 检验。\n    expected_results:\n      classification_f1_mean: 0.873\n      classification_f1_std: 0.003\n      cwm_f1_mean: 0.793\n      cwm_f1_std: 0.008\n      gap_mean_pp: 8.0\n      gap_std_pp: 0.9\n      paired_ttest_p: 0.008\n      significant_at_005: true\n      bootstrap_95ci_gap_lower_pp: 5.2\n      bootstrap_95ci_gap_upper_pp: 10.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Classification 任务输出空间为二元标签，收敛行为稳定，seed 间方差小（std ~0.3pp）。\n      CWM 方差更大（std ~0.8pp），因为 generation 质量对初始化更敏感——不同 seed 学到的\n      输出格式化模式略有差异，导致 string matching 成功率波动。\n      3 个 seed 的 paired t-test 自由度只有 2，p=0.008 刚好通过 0.05 阈值，但审稿人可能\n      质疑样本量。Bootstrap CI 下界 5.2pp 仍大于 3pp kill 线，确认 gap 稳健。\n      median 档下这个结果足以支撑论文，但不如 best 档那样压倒性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Multi-Seed Stability\"\n        columns: [Formulation, Seed_0, Seed_1, Seed_42, Mean, Std]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification, 0.876, 0.870, 0.873, 0.873, 0.003]\n          - [CWM Generation, 0.801, 0.785, 0.793, 0.793, 0.008]\n          - [\"Gap (pp)\", 7.5, 8.5, 8.0, 8.0, 0.9]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot: 3-seed F1 分布对比，classification 箱体窄，CWM 箱体宽\"\n    analysis: >\n      Gap 显著（p<0.01），CI 下界 > kill 线。但 n=3 seeds 的统计效力有限，审稿人可能要求更多 seeds。\n      Median 档下建议在 limitation 中承认样本量约束。\n\n  - name: \"Trace-then-Judge Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"trace-then-judge\"\n    description: >\n      单 Qwen3-4B 模型训练先生成 ~50 token 执行推理 trace，再输出 pass/fail（CoT 风格）。\n      隔离分类优势来源：是跳过 trace 本身有用，还是任务简化有用？\n    expected_results:\n      ttj_pass_f1: 0.81\n      ttj_fail_f1: 0.82\n      ttj_avg_f1: 0.815\n      ttj_accuracy: 0.82\n      ttj_vs_classification_gap_pp: -5.8\n      ttj_vs_cwm_gap_pp: 2.0\n      trace_quality_exact_match: 0.45\n      trace_quality_semantic_correct: 0.68\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trace-then-Judge 的 F1 (~81.5%) 落在 CWM (79.5%) 和 classification (87.5%) 之间，\n      这是 median 档最核心的 confound。两种解读都有道理：\n      (a) \"trace 有帮助\"：TtJ 比 CWM 高 2pp，说明先推理再分类比直接生成输出好，支撑\n      \"分类是更好的最终判定方式\"。\n      (b) \"trace 有害\"：TtJ 比 direct classification 低 5.8pp，说明强制生成 trace 引入了\n      不必要的噪声——模型有时生成错误 trace 但据此做出错误判断，或生成正确 trace 但\n      提取 pass/fail 时出错。\n      这个结果无法干净分离 \"formulation advantage\" 和 \"task simplicity advantage\"，\n      因为 TtJ 同时包含两者的混合效应。论文必须诚实讨论这个 confound，不能简单声称\n      classification 的优势完全来自 formulation。\n      trace 质量分析显示只有 45% exact match 和 68% 语义正确，解释了为何 TtJ 未能达到\n      classification 水平——trace 生成本身就是一个困难的中间任务。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Formulation Spectrum\"\n        columns: [Method, Avg_F1, \"vs Classification\", \"vs CWM\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification (direct), 0.875, \"-\", \"+8.0pp\"]\n          - [Trace-then-Judge, 0.815, \"-6.0pp\", \"+2.0pp\"]\n          - [CWM Generation, 0.795, \"-8.0pp\", \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 三种 formulation 的 F1 对比，error bar 来自 multi-seed（如果有）\"\n      - \"Confusion matrix 对比: TtJ 中 trace-correct-but-judge-wrong vs trace-wrong-but-judge-right 的交叉分析\"\n    analysis: >\n      TtJ 位于两者之间是 median 档的关键特征。论文不能简单画 classification > TtJ > CWM 的递进关系，\n      因为 TtJ 的 CoT 设计与 CWM 的 full output generation 是不同的中间点。\n      建议在论文中呈现为 \"execution reasoning provides partial benefit, but the overhead of\n      trace generation outweighs the reasoning advantage compared to direct classification.\"\n\n  - name: \"Trajectory-Level Fine-tuned Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"traj-level-finetuned\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B LoRA 训练 trajectory-level resolved/unresolved 预测。隔离 granularity 效应。\n    expected_results:\n      traj_accuracy: 0.835\n      traj_resolved_f1: 0.83\n      traj_unresolved_f1: 0.84\n      traj_avg_f1: 0.835\n      per_test_vs_traj_gap_pp: 4.0\n      traj_context_length_median_tokens: 2800\n      per_test_context_length_median_tokens: 850\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trajectory-level 将所有测试拼接为单一输入，输出 resolved/unresolved 二元标签。\n      任务本身仍是分类（非 generation），但上下文更长（中位 ~2800 tokens vs per-test ~850 tokens）\n      且需要隐式推理所有测试的聚合结果。\n      F1 ~83.5% 介于 per-test (87.5%) 和 CWM (79.5%) 之间，但更接近 per-test。\n      4pp gap 来自两个因素：(1) 长上下文降低了 4B 模型的注意力效率，部分测试信息被丢失；\n      (2) 聚合预测要求模型隐式执行 \"any test fails → unresolved\" 的逻辑，而 per-test 模型\n      只需逐个判断。\n      这个结果表明 granularity 贡献了 ~4pp（per-test vs traj），formulation 贡献了 ~4pp\n      （traj vs CWM），两者大致等分了 8pp 总 gap。这是一个有趣的分解，但也使得\n      \"task reformulation\" 的叙事需要更精确——不能将全部优势归于 formulation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Granularity vs Formulation Decomposition\"\n        columns: [Method, Formulation, Granularity, Avg_F1, Gap_Source]\n        rows:\n          - [Per-test Classification, Classification, Per-test, 0.875, \"Reference\"]\n          - [Trajectory Classification, Classification, Trajectory, 0.835, \"Granularity: -4.0pp\"]\n          - [CWM Generation, Generation, Per-test, 0.795, \"Formulation: -4.0pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2x2 matrix heatmap: formulation (x) × granularity (y) → F1，显示两个因素的独立贡献\"\n    analysis: >\n      Granularity 和 formulation 各贡献 ~4pp，意味着论文 Claim 1 不能仅强调 formulation——\n      必须承认 per-test granularity 本身也带来了显著增益。\n      建议将 Claim 1 改写为 \"classification formulation AND per-test granularity jointly provide...\"\n\n  - name: \"Model Size Scaling (4B → 8B)\"\n    plan_id: \"model-size-scaling\"\n    description: >\n      Classification 和 CWM 均扩展到 8B，观察 gap 是否随规模缩小。\n    expected_results:\n      classification_8b_f1: 0.895\n      cwm_8b_f1: 0.84\n      gap_8b_pp: 5.5\n      gap_4b_pp: 8.0\n      gap_narrowing_pp: 2.5\n      classification_4b_to_8b_gain_pp: 2.0\n      cwm_4b_to_8b_gain_pp: 4.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      8B 模型容量更大，CWM 获益更多（+4.5pp vs classification +2.0pp），因为额外参数主要帮助\n      解决 generation 的瓶颈——更好的输出格式化、更准确的字符串预测、更少的 token exhaustion。\n      Classification 已经在 4B 达到较高水平（87.5%），改进空间本就有限。\n      Gap 从 8pp 缩小到 5.5pp，支撑 median 档叙事：\"classification advantage may narrow\n      at larger scales\"。但 5.5pp 仍然显著，说明 formulation difference 不会被纯粹的\n      scale 抹平——至少在 4B-8B 范围内。\n      推测在 32B+ 规模下 gap 可能进一步收窄到 2-3pp，但本实验无法验证。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Scaling Behavior\"\n        columns: [Model_Size, Classification_F1, CWM_F1, Gap_pp]\n        rows:\n          - [4B, 0.875, 0.795, 8.0]\n          - [8B, 0.895, 0.840, 5.5]\n          - [Delta, \"+2.0pp\", \"+4.5pp\", \"-2.5pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: x=model_size, y=F1, 两条线（classification vs CWM），显示 gap 收敛趋势\"\n    analysis: >\n      Gap 收窄但仍显著，是 median 档的典型结果。论文可以画一条外推虚线暗示更大模型可能收敛，\n      但不应做强断言。这个结果使 Claim 1 的 framing 必须包含 \"at small model scales\" 的限定词。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Test Failure Precision/Recall\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-precision-recall\"\n    description: >\n      在完整测试集上衡量 per-test failure 预测的 precision 和 recall。\n    expected_results:\n      failure_precision: 0.78\n      failure_recall: 0.74\n      failure_f1: 0.76\n      pass_precision: 0.88\n      pass_recall: 0.90\n      false_positive_rate: 0.10\n      false_negative_rate: 0.26\n      precision_at_k3_failures: 0.72\n      ndcg_failure_ranking: 0.81\n    result_rationale: >\n      模型在预测\"哪些测试会失败\"上的 precision ~78% 意味着每 5 个 failure 预测中有 ~1 个是\n      false positive（实际 pass 的测试被错误标记为 fail）。Recall ~74% 意味着 ~26% 的真实\n      failure 被漏掉。\n      这种不对称是合理的：(a) pass 类更多（数据分布 52% pass），模型对 pass 的预测更有信心；\n      (b) failure 模式多样（assertion error, exception, timeout），部分 edge case 难以从\n      代码静态分析推断。\n      78% precision 对下游 re-repair 的含义是：repair agent 收到的 failure 信息有 ~22% 噪声，\n      可能导致修复方向偏移。这解释了为什么 re-repair lift 在 median 档只有 ~2.5%。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Diagnostic Signal Quality\"\n        columns: [Metric, Value]\n        rows:\n          - [Failure Precision, 0.78]\n          - [Failure Recall, 0.74]\n          - [Failure F1, 0.76]\n          - [Pass Precision, 0.88]\n          - [Pass Recall, 0.90]\n          - [False Positive Rate, 0.10]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Precision-Recall curve for failure class, 标注 operating point\"\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap: predicted vs actual pass/fail\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 Claim 2 的前提实验。78%/74% 的 precision/recall 表明 diagnostic signal 存在但有噪声。\n      足以作为 \"signal quality analysis\" 的正面结果，但不足以支撑 \"actionable diagnostics\" 的强叙事。\n      建议论文讨论 precision 阈值——在什么 precision 下 per-test info 开始帮助 vs 误导 repair agent。\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Re-Repair Pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: >\n      200 实例上对比：repair agent 有 per-test failure 预测 vs 无 per-test 信息，比较 resolve rate。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_resolve_rate: 0.32\n      with_pertest_resolve_rate: 0.345\n      resolve_rate_lift_pct: 2.5\n      lift_absolute_instances: 5\n      p_value_mcnemar: 0.12\n      significant_at_005: false\n      significant_at_010: false\n      n_instances: 200\n      effect_size_cohens_h: 0.05\n      power_at_n200: 0.28\n    result_rationale: >\n      2.5% resolve rate lift（32% → 34.5%）在 n=200 下不显著（p=0.12）。\n      效应量极小（Cohen's h=0.05），统计检验功效只有 28%——需要 n≈2000 才能在 α=0.05 下\n      检测到这个 effect size。\n      lift 之所以小有三个原因：\n      (1) 69% 的实例只有 T=1 F2P 测试，per-test info 退化为 trajectory-level，无额外信息；\n      (2) 78% precision 意味着 ~22% 的 failure 预测是错误的，repair agent 有时被误导；\n      (3) 当前 repair agent（SWE-agent 级别）的 re-repair 能力有限，即使给出正确的 failure\n      定位，也不一定能修复。\n      这个结果在 median 档下是 \"suggestive but inconclusive\"——方向正确但证据不足。\n      论文应呈现为 pilot study，承认 underpowered，建议未来工作用更大样本验证。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Re-Repair Pilot Results\"\n        columns: [Condition, Resolve_Rate, N, \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [No per-test info, \"32.0%\", 200, \"[25.6%, 38.4%]\"]\n          - [With per-test predictions, \"34.5%\", 200, \"[27.9%, 41.1%]\"]\n          - [Lift, \"+2.5pp\", \"-\", \"p=0.12 (n.s.)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart with error bars: resolve rate ± 95% CI，两个条件\"\n      - \"Stratified lift by T: T=1 instances (lift ≈ 0%) vs T≥2 instances (lift ≈ 6-8%)\"\n    analysis: >\n      不显著的 re-repair lift 是 median 档对 Claim 2 的最大打击。论文策略：\n      (1) 将 per-test-precision-recall 作为 Claim 2 的主要证据（signal 存在）；\n      (2) re-repair 降级为 pilot/suggestive evidence；\n      (3) 展示 T≥2 子集的 stratified lift（预计 6-8%）作为 \"per-test info helps when it\n      provides new information\" 的支撑。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle F2P Stratified Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"oracle-f2p-stratified\"\n    description: >\n      按 F2P 测试数量 T=1, T=2, T=3+ 分层，报告 per-test vs trajectory 的 oracle advantage。\n    expected_results:\n      T1_pct_instances: 0.69\n      T1_iid_advantage: 0.02\n      T1_block_advantage: 0.05\n      T2_pct_instances: 0.19\n      T2_iid_advantage: 0.09\n      T2_block_advantage: 0.22\n      T3plus_pct_instances: 0.12\n      T3plus_iid_advantage: 0.18\n      T3plus_block_advantage: 0.38\n      population_weighted_iid_advantage: 0.046\n      population_weighted_block_advantage: 0.115\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 oracle 模拟的直接分解，结果由数学性质决定而非模型训练。\n      T=1 时 per-test 和 trajectory-level 在数学上几乎等价——唯一差异来自 per-test 模型\n      在该测试上的 calibration 可能不同于 trajectory 模型的整体 calibration。优势 ~2%。\n      T=2 时 per-test 可以区分\"两个测试都失败\"和\"只有一个测试失败\"的 patch，提供了\n      trajectory-level 无法获得的排序信号。i.i.d. 优势 ~9%，block-corr 下 ~22%。\n      T=3+ 时优势最大（i.i.d. 18%, block 38%），因为更多测试提供了更丰富的 ranking 信号。\n      但 T=3+ 只占 12% 的实例，所以 population-weighted advantage 被严重稀释。\n      Block correlation 在所有 T 下都放大优势，因为 correlated errors 降低了 effective\n      独立测试数，使每个测试的信息量更大。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Stratified Oracle Advantage\"\n        columns: [T_bucket, Pct_Instances, IID_Advantage, Block_Advantage]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T=1\", \"69%\", \"2.0%\", \"5.0%\"]\n          - [\"T=2\", \"19%\", \"9.0%\", \"22.0%\"]\n          - [\"T≥3\", \"12%\", \"18.0%\", \"38.0%\"]\n          - [\"Pop. Weighted\", \"100%\", \"4.6%\", \"11.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: per-T bucket advantage, i.i.d. vs block, 颜色区分\"\n      - \"Stacked area: SWE-bench T 分布直方图，叠加 per-test advantage 曲线\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 Claim 3 的核心表格，也是论文最强贡献。清晰展示 per-test advantage 集中在\n      T≥2 实例（31%），为 \"when to deploy per-test simulation\" 提供了 actionable decision rule。\n      建议论文标题或副标题直接引用这个发现。\n\n  - name: \"Block Correlation Empirical Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"block-corr-empirical\"\n    description: >\n      从训练好的 classification 模型的 test-level 预测中测量误差相关结构，\n      与 i.i.d. 和 block-corr 模拟对比。\n    expected_results:\n      empirical_spearman_vs_iid: 0.18\n      empirical_spearman_vs_block: 0.72\n      effective_rho: 0.22\n      ratio_to_block_model_rho: 0.44\n      iid_model_ks_test_p: 0.003\n      block_model_ks_test_p: 0.08\n    result_rationale: >\n      模型预测误差在同一 instance 内存在中等程度相关（Spearman vs i.i.d. = 0.18），\n      因为共享的代码上下文导致类似的 failure 模式（如模型对某种 assertion 风格系统性判错）。\n      但这种相关远低于 block model 假设的完全相关（Spearman vs block = 0.72）。\n      实际 effective rho ~0.22 大约是 block model rho 的 44%。\n      KS 检验显示 i.i.d. 模型被显著拒绝（p=0.003），block model 未被拒绝（p=0.08）\n      但也不算好的 fit。真实误差结构介于两者之间，更接近 i.i.d.。\n      这意味着 oracle 模拟中 block-corr 结果是上界估计，i.i.d. 结果更接近现实。\n      对论文叙事的影响：population-weighted advantage 的 realistic estimate 更接近\n      4.6%（i.i.d.）而非 11.5%（block），降低了 per-test 的整体优势主张。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Error Correlation Structure\"\n        columns: [Metric, Empirical, IID_Model, Block_Model]\n        rows:\n          - [Intra-instance error Spearman, 0.18, 0.0, 1.0]\n          - [Effective ρ, 0.22, 0.0, 0.50]\n          - [KS test p-value, \"-\", 0.003, 0.08]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: empirical error correlation matrix (test-pair) vs predicted under i.i.d. and block models\"\n    analysis: >\n      实证数据确认误差结构介于两个极端之间，effective T 更接近 i.i.d.。\n      这是论文诚实性的体现——block model 结果虽然好看，但不是最佳估计。\n      建议报告 calibrated advantage（插值 i.i.d. 和 block 结果）作为 point estimate。\n\n  - name: \"SWE-bench PerTest Data Construction\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: >\n      Docker 重跑 SWE-bench Verified 的 patch，提取 per-test pass/fail 标签。\n      目标 500 instances × 16 candidates。\n    expected_results:\n      target_instances: 500\n      successful_instances: 420\n      failed_instances: 80\n      failure_rate: 0.16\n      failure_reasons:\n        docker_timeout: 35\n        env_setup_failure: 25\n        flaky_tests: 12\n        other: 8\n      total_candidate_test_pairs: 67200\n      avg_tests_per_instance: 42\n      avg_f2p_per_instance: 2.8\n      avg_p2p_per_instance: 39.2\n      compute_hours_wall: 22\n    result_rationale: >\n      16% 失败率反映 SWE-bench Docker 环境的现实复杂度。主要失败原因：\n      (1) Docker timeout（35 例）：部分 repo 的测试套件耗时超过容器限制，尤其是大型 Django/scipy 项目；\n      (2) 环境搭建失败（25 例）：依赖版本冲突、系统库缺失、Python 版本不匹配；\n      (3) Flaky tests（12 例）：测试结果在重跑间不一致，无法作为可靠标签。\n      420 个成功实例 × 16 candidates = 6720 instance-candidate pairs，每个平均 ~42 个测试，\n      总计 ~67k test-level labels。这个数据量足以支撑 repo-level 训练实验。\n      22h wall clock 在 16 并行容器下合理（~1.3h per instance 平均，考虑排队和重试）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Data statistics dashboard: instances per repo, T distribution histogram, failure mode breakdown\"\n    analysis: >\n      420 个实例（vs 目标 500）是可接受的 yield。更关键的是数据质量——需要验证 flaky test\n      过滤是否充分，以及 per-test labels 与官方 SWE-bench 的 trajectory-level labels 一致性。\n\n  - name: \"Repo-Level Training\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: >\n      在 SWE-bench-PerTest 数据上微调 Qwen3-4B/8B，预测 repo-level per-test pass/fail。\n    expected_results:\n      repo_4b_pass_f1: 0.72\n      repo_4b_fail_f1: 0.75\n      repo_4b_avg_f1: 0.735\n      repo_4b_accuracy: 0.74\n      repo_8b_pass_f1: 0.77\n      repo_8b_fail_f1: 0.79\n      repo_8b_avg_f1: 0.78\n      repo_8b_accuracy: 0.78\n      function_to_repo_drop_4b_pp: 14.0\n      function_to_repo_drop_8b_pp: 11.5\n      context_length_median_tokens: 4200\n      context_length_p95_tokens: 12800\n    result_rationale: >\n      Repo-level per-class F1 ~73.5% (4B) / ~78% (8B) 反映了 repo-level 任务的固有难度：\n      (1) 上下文长度大幅增加（中位 ~4200 tokens，P95 ~12800 tokens），超过 function-level 的\n      ~850 tokens 约 5 倍，4B 模型的注意力容量受限；\n      (2) 跨文件依赖要求模型理解 import 链、类继承、配置文件的影响，这在 function-level 不存在；\n      (3) 训练数据量更少（420 instances vs function-level 数千条），过拟合风险更高；\n      (4) 测试复杂度更高——repo-level 测试常涉及 fixture setup、database state、file I/O。\n      8B 模型比 4B 好 ~4.5pp，主要得益于更好的长上下文处理能力。\n      14pp drop（function → repo）对论文的影响：不能直接将 function-level 的结论泛化到 repo-level，\n      需要在论文中作为 separate evaluation 呈现，并诚实讨论 generalization gap。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Function-Level vs Repo-Level\"\n        columns: [Level, Model, Avg_F1, Accuracy]\n        rows:\n          - [Function, 4B, 0.875, 0.875]\n          - [Function, 8B, 0.895, 0.895]\n          - [Repo, 4B, 0.735, 0.740]\n          - [Repo, 8B, 0.780, 0.780]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar: function vs repo F1, 4B vs 8B, 误差条表示 per-repo 方差\"\n    analysis: >\n      Repo-level F1 在 median 档 [70-79] 范围内。结果 usable 但不 impressive。\n      论文策略：作为 \"preliminary extension\" 呈现，强调 function-level 是主要贡献，\n      repo-level 展示方法可行性但需要更多数据和更大模型。\n\n  - name: \"LLM-as-Judge Baselines\"\n    plan_id: \"llm-judge-baseline\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-8B/32B zero-shot LLM-as-judge，trajectory-level 和 per-test 两种模式。\n      作为 Pareto frontier 的参考点。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen3_8b_traj_accuracy: 0.65\n      qwen3_8b_pertest_accuracy: 0.62\n      qwen3_32b_traj_accuracy: 0.72\n      qwen3_32b_pertest_accuracy: 0.69\n      qwen3_8b_traj_f1: 0.63\n      qwen3_32b_traj_f1: 0.71\n      qwen3_8b_pertest_f1: 0.60\n      qwen3_32b_pertest_f1: 0.67\n      inference_cost_8b_per_instance_sec: 2.5\n      inference_cost_32b_per_instance_sec: 12.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Zero-shot LLM judge 缺乏 task-specific fine-tuning 信号，必须依赖通用代码理解能力。\n      8B zero-shot (~63% F1) 远低于 4B fine-tuned (~87.5%)，说明 fine-tuning 在这个任务上\n      价值巨大——通用代码理解不足以可靠预测执行结果。\n      32B 通过更强的代码推理能力达到 ~71% F1，但仍低于 fine-tuned 4B。\n      Per-test 模式比 trajectory 略差 2-3pp，因为 per-test 需要更精细的推理（判断单个测试的\n      具体行为），而 trajectory-level 可以利用更多启发式规则（如\"代码改动小 → 大概率 pass\"）。\n      这些 baseline 在 Pareto frontier 上提供了 \"high cost, moderate accuracy\" 的参考点，\n      与 fine-tuned classification 的 \"low cost, high accuracy\" 形成清晰对比。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: Pareto Frontier Reference Points\"\n        columns: [Model, Mode, Params, Fine-tuned, F1, Cost_per_instance]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-4B LoRA, Per-test Classification, 4B, Yes, 0.875, \"0.3s\"]\n          - [Qwen3-4B LoRA, CWM Generation, 4B, Yes, 0.795, \"0.8s\"]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, \"Zero-shot Traj\", 8B, No, 0.63, \"2.5s\"]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, \"Zero-shot Per-test\", 8B, No, 0.60, \"2.5s\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, \"Zero-shot Traj\", 32B, No, 0.71, \"12s\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, \"Zero-shot Per-test\", 32B, No, 0.67, \"12s\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto frontier scatter: x=cost (inference time), y=F1, 每个方法一个点，Pareto 前沿线\"\n    analysis: >\n      Fine-tuned 4B classification 在 Pareto frontier 上占据最优位置——最低成本且最高精度。\n      这个结果强化了 Claim 1 的实用性论点：不仅 formulation 更好，还更高效。\n      32B zero-shot 接近但未超过 4B fine-tuned CWM，有趣但不意外。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Test Majority Voting (K=3)\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-majority-voting\"\n    description: >\n      Classification 模型 K=3 self-consistency，测试多数投票是否提升 per-test 精度。\n    expected_results:\n      single_pass_f1: 0.875\n      majority_k3_f1: 0.885\n      improvement_pp: 1.0\n      compute_multiplier: 3.0\n      marginal_gain_per_compute: 0.33\n      agreement_rate_k3: 0.92\n      flip_rate_correct_to_wrong: 0.02\n      flip_rate_wrong_to_correct: 0.04\n    result_rationale: >\n      Majority voting 带来 ~1pp 改进（87.5% → 88.5%），因为 classification 任务已经在\n      单次推理下达到较高 calibration。92% 的样本三次预测完全一致，意味着大部分 uncertainty\n      已经在单次推理中被解决。\n      剩余 8% 不一致的样本中，4% 从错误翻转为正确（2:1 多数），2% 从正确翻转为错误（1:2 少数）。\n      净增益 = 4% - 2% = 2%，但由于只影响 8% 的样本，总体改进 ≈ 2% × 8% / (scale) ≈ 1pp。\n      3 倍推理成本换取 1pp 改进，成本效益比低。论文可以在 appendix 中报告但不作为主要结果。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A1 (Appendix): Self-Consistency\"\n        columns: [K, F1, Compute, Marginal_Gain_per_Compute]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.875, \"1×\", \"-\"]\n          - [3, 0.885, \"3×\", \"0.33pp/×\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      边际收益递减，确认 classification formulation 已经达到该模型规模下的近最优预测。\n      这间接支撑了 Claim 1——classification 不需要额外 test-time compute tricks 就能达到高精度。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2131,"cache_read_input_tokens":45680,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2131},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e2ff9bf-0df6-4a54-a6c1-9e43e44e7de7","uuid":"152f204a-e83e-4353-a9b1-5194208bd6cc"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":312453,"duration_api_ms":313298,"num_turns":11,"result":"Now I have all the context needed. Let me produce the detailed median-tier imagined experiments.\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claim 1 降调: classification 在 4B 规模下有 5-10pp F1 优势，但不能说 \"fundamentally simpler\"，\n  改为 \"favorable accuracy-efficiency tradeoff at small model scales\"。Trace-then-Judge 落在\n  classification 和 CWM 之间，confound 无法干净分离——需要诚实讨论。\n  Claim 2 弱化: per-test precision/recall 尚可但非压倒性（~78%/74%），re-repair lift ~2.5% 在\n  n=200 下不显著，作为 pilot evidence 而非 main result。\n  Claim 3 成为论文最强贡献: oracle frontier 分析 + stratified T 分析 + block correlation 实测\n  提供清晰的 decision framework。\n  整体 reframe 为 \"When and Why Per-Test Simulation Helps\"，以 Claim 3 的 characterization 为主轴，\n  Claim 1 的 classification advantage 为支撑。EMNLP Findings 更稳妥，Main 需要 Claim 2 突破或\n  Claim 3 叙事特别精彩。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"CWM Generation Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"cwm-baseline\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B LoRA 训练预测执行输出（generation），同数据同配置对比 classification (87.1/87.9% F1)。\n    expected_results:\n      cwm_pass_f1: 0.79\n      cwm_fail_f1: 0.80\n      cwm_overall_accuracy: 0.795\n      cwm_per_class_f1_avg: 0.795\n      classification_minus_cwm_gap_pp: 7.8\n      cwm_token_budget_exhaust_rate: 0.12\n      cwm_string_mismatch_rate: 0.18\n    result_rationale: >\n      CWM 在简单 assertion 测试（assertEqual, assertTrue）上表现接近 classification，因为输出\n      短且可预测。但在复杂输出场景下显著退化：(1) ~12% 的样本因输出超过 LoRA 微调时的 max_new_tokens\n      而被截断，导致无法提取正确答案；(2) ~18% 的样本因字符串值预测错误（浮点精度、格式差异、\n      动态值如时间戳）而判错。这两个失败模式正是 Debugging CWMs 论文指出的核心问题。\n      4B 模型容量有限，无法同时学好\"理解代码语义\"和\"精确生成输出字符串\"，导致 per-class F1\n      落在 79-80%，比 classification 低约 8pp。这个 gap 处于 moderate 范围——足以支撑\n      \"classification 有优势\"的叙事，但不足以称为 \"fundamentally simpler\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Classification vs Generation (4B, Function-level)\"\n        columns: [Model, Formulation, Pass_F1, Fail_F1, Avg_F1, Accuracy]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-4B LoRA, Classification, 0.871, 0.879, 0.875, 0.875]\n          - [Qwen3-4B LoRA, \"CWM Generation\", 0.79, 0.80, 0.795, 0.795]\n          - [Delta, \"-\", \"+8.1pp\", \"+7.9pp\", \"+8.0pp\", \"+8.0pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Error analysis pie chart: CWM failure modes 分解 — token exhaustion 12%, string mismatch 18%, semantic error 70%\"\n    analysis: >\n      8pp gap 在 median 档是 make-or-break 的边界值。需要 multi-seed 验证确认 gap 稳定且显著。\n      如果 multi-seed 方差大到 CI 包含 3pp（kill 线），论文核心论点受威胁。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-Seed Core Comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"multi-seed-core\"\n    description: >\n      Classification 和 CWM 各 3 个 seed {0, 1, 42}，报告 mean ± std，paired t-test 检验。\n    expected_results:\n      classification_f1_mean: 0.873\n      classification_f1_std: 0.003\n      cwm_f1_mean: 0.793\n      cwm_f1_std: 0.008\n      gap_mean_pp: 8.0\n      gap_std_pp: 0.9\n      paired_ttest_p: 0.008\n      significant_at_005: true\n      bootstrap_95ci_gap_lower_pp: 5.2\n      bootstrap_95ci_gap_upper_pp: 10.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Classification 任务输出空间为二元标签，收敛行为稳定，seed 间方差小（std ~0.3pp）。\n      CWM 方差更大（std ~0.8pp），因为 generation 质量对初始化更敏感——不同 seed 学到的\n      输出格式化模式略有差异，导致 string matching 成功率波动。\n      3 个 seed 的 paired t-test 自由度只有 2，p=0.008 刚好通过 0.05 阈值，但审稿人可能\n      质疑样本量。Bootstrap CI 下界 5.2pp 仍大于 3pp kill 线，确认 gap 稳健。\n      median 档下这个结果足以支撑论文，但不如 best 档那样压倒性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Multi-Seed Stability\"\n        columns: [Formulation, Seed_0, Seed_1, Seed_42, Mean, Std]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification, 0.876, 0.870, 0.873, 0.873, 0.003]\n          - [CWM Generation, 0.801, 0.785, 0.793, 0.793, 0.008]\n          - [\"Gap (pp)\", 7.5, 8.5, 8.0, 8.0, 0.9]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot: 3-seed F1 分布对比，classification 箱体窄，CWM 箱体宽\"\n    analysis: >\n      Gap 显著（p<0.01），CI 下界 > kill 线。但 n=3 seeds 的统计效力有限，审稿人可能要求更多 seeds。\n      Median 档下建议在 limitation 中承认样本量约束。\n\n  - name: \"Trace-then-Judge Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"trace-then-judge\"\n    description: >\n      单 Qwen3-4B 模型训练先生成 ~50 token 执行推理 trace，再输出 pass/fail（CoT 风格）。\n      隔离分类优势来源：是跳过 trace 本身有用，还是任务简化有用？\n    expected_results:\n      ttj_pass_f1: 0.81\n      ttj_fail_f1: 0.82\n      ttj_avg_f1: 0.815\n      ttj_accuracy: 0.82\n      ttj_vs_classification_gap_pp: -5.8\n      ttj_vs_cwm_gap_pp: 2.0\n      trace_quality_exact_match: 0.45\n      trace_quality_semantic_correct: 0.68\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trace-then-Judge 的 F1 (~81.5%) 落在 CWM (79.5%) 和 classification (87.5%) 之间，\n      这是 median 档最核心的 confound。两种解读都有道理：\n      (a) \"trace 有帮助\"：TtJ 比 CWM 高 2pp，说明先推理再分类比直接生成输出好，支撑\n      \"分类是更好的最终判定方式\"。\n      (b) \"trace 有害\"：TtJ 比 direct classification 低 5.8pp，说明强制生成 trace 引入了\n      不必要的噪声——模型有时生成错误 trace 但据此做出错误判断，或生成正确 trace 但\n      提取 pass/fail 时出错。\n      这个结果无法干净分离 \"formulation advantage\" 和 \"task simplicity advantage\"，\n      因为 TtJ 同时包含两者的混合效应。论文必须诚实讨论这个 confound，不能简单声称\n      classification 的优势完全来自 formulation。\n      trace 质量分析显示只有 45% exact match 和 68% 语义正确，解释了为何 TtJ 未能达到\n      classification 水平——trace 生成本身就是一个困难的中间任务。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Formulation Spectrum\"\n        columns: [Method, Avg_F1, \"vs Classification\", \"vs CWM\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Classification (direct), 0.875, \"-\", \"+8.0pp\"]\n          - [Trace-then-Judge, 0.815, \"-6.0pp\", \"+2.0pp\"]\n          - [CWM Generation, 0.795, \"-8.0pp\", \"-\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: 三种 formulation 的 F1 对比，error bar 来自 multi-seed（如果有）\"\n      - \"Confusion matrix 对比: TtJ 中 trace-correct-but-judge-wrong vs trace-wrong-but-judge-right 的交叉分析\"\n    analysis: >\n      TtJ 位于两者之间是 median 档的关键特征。论文不能简单画 classification > TtJ > CWM 的递进关系，\n      因为 TtJ 的 CoT 设计与 CWM 的 full output generation 是不同的中间点。\n      建议在论文中呈现为 \"execution reasoning provides partial benefit, but the overhead of\n      trace generation outweighs the reasoning advantage compared to direct classification.\"\n\n  - name: \"Trajectory-Level Fine-tuned Baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"traj-level-finetuned\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-4B LoRA 训练 trajectory-level resolved/unresolved 预测。隔离 granularity 效应。\n    expected_results:\n      traj_accuracy: 0.835\n      traj_resolved_f1: 0.83\n      traj_unresolved_f1: 0.84\n      traj_avg_f1: 0.835\n      per_test_vs_traj_gap_pp: 4.0\n      traj_context_length_median_tokens: 2800\n      per_test_context_length_median_tokens: 850\n    result_rationale: >\n      Trajectory-level 将所有测试拼接为单一输入，输出 resolved/unresolved 二元标签。\n      任务本身仍是分类（非 generation），但上下文更长（中位 ~2800 tokens vs per-test ~850 tokens）\n      且需要隐式推理所有测试的聚合结果。\n      F1 ~83.5% 介于 per-test (87.5%) 和 CWM (79.5%) 之间，但更接近 per-test。\n      4pp gap 来自两个因素：(1) 长上下文降低了 4B 模型的注意力效率，部分测试信息被丢失；\n      (2) 聚合预测要求模型隐式执行 \"any test fails → unresolved\" 的逻辑，而 per-test 模型\n      只需逐个判断。\n      这个结果表明 granularity 贡献了 ~4pp（per-test vs traj），formulation 贡献了 ~4pp\n      （traj vs CWM），两者大致等分了 8pp 总 gap。这是一个有趣的分解，但也使得\n      \"task reformulation\" 的叙事需要更精确——不能将全部优势归于 formulation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Granularity vs Formulation Decomposition\"\n        columns: [Method, Formulation, Granularity, Avg_F1, Gap_Source]\n        rows:\n          - [Per-test Classification, Classification, Per-test, 0.875, \"Reference\"]\n          - [Trajectory Classification, Classification, Trajectory, 0.835, \"Granularity: -4.0pp\"]\n          - [CWM Generation, Generation, Per-test, 0.795, \"Formulation: -4.0pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2x2 matrix heatmap: formulation (x) × granularity (y) → F1，显示两个因素的独立贡献\"\n    analysis: >\n      Granularity 和 formulation 各贡献 ~4pp，意味着论文 Claim 1 不能仅强调 formulation——\n      必须承认 per-test granularity 本身也带来了显著增益。\n      建议将 Claim 1 改写为 \"classification formulation AND per-test granularity jointly provide...\"\n\n  - name: \"Model Size Scaling (4B → 8B)\"\n    plan_id: \"model-size-scaling\"\n    description: >\n      Classification 和 CWM 均扩展到 8B，观察 gap 是否随规模缩小。\n    expected_results:\n      classification_8b_f1: 0.895\n      cwm_8b_f1: 0.84\n      gap_8b_pp: 5.5\n      gap_4b_pp: 8.0\n      gap_narrowing_pp: 2.5\n      classification_4b_to_8b_gain_pp: 2.0\n      cwm_4b_to_8b_gain_pp: 4.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      8B 模型容量更大，CWM 获益更多（+4.5pp vs classification +2.0pp），因为额外参数主要帮助\n      解决 generation 的瓶颈——更好的输出格式化、更准确的字符串预测、更少的 token exhaustion。\n      Classification 已经在 4B 达到较高水平（87.5%），改进空间本就有限。\n      Gap 从 8pp 缩小到 5.5pp，支撑 median 档叙事：\"classification advantage may narrow\n      at larger scales\"。但 5.5pp 仍然显著，说明 formulation difference 不会被纯粹的\n      scale 抹平——至少在 4B-8B 范围内。\n      推测在 32B+ 规模下 gap 可能进一步收窄到 2-3pp，但本实验无法验证。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Scaling Behavior\"\n        columns: [Model_Size, Classification_F1, CWM_F1, Gap_pp]\n        rows:\n          - [4B, 0.875, 0.795, 8.0]\n          - [8B, 0.895, 0.840, 5.5]\n          - [Delta, \"+2.0pp\", \"+4.5pp\", \"-2.5pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: x=model_size, y=F1, 两条线（classification vs CWM），显示 gap 收敛趋势\"\n    analysis: >\n      Gap 收窄但仍显著，是 median 档的典型结果。论文可以画一条外推虚线暗示更大模型可能收敛，\n      但不应做强断言。这个结果使 Claim 1 的 framing 必须包含 \"at small model scales\" 的限定词。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Test Failure Precision/Recall\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-precision-recall\"\n    description: >\n      在完整测试集上衡量 per-test failure 预测的 precision 和 recall。\n    expected_results:\n      failure_precision: 0.78\n      failure_recall: 0.74\n      failure_f1: 0.76\n      pass_precision: 0.88\n      pass_recall: 0.90\n      false_positive_rate: 0.10\n      false_negative_rate: 0.26\n      precision_at_k3_failures: 0.72\n      ndcg_failure_ranking: 0.81\n    result_rationale: >\n      模型在预测\"哪些测试会失败\"上的 precision ~78% 意味着每 5 个 failure 预测中有 ~1 个是\n      false positive（实际 pass 的测试被错误标记为 fail）。Recall ~74% 意味着 ~26% 的真实\n      failure 被漏掉。\n      这种不对称是合理的：(a) pass 类更多（数据分布 52% pass），模型对 pass 的预测更有信心；\n      (b) failure 模式多样（assertion error, exception, timeout），部分 edge case 难以从\n      代码静态分析推断。\n      78% precision 对下游 re-repair 的含义是：repair agent 收到的 failure 信息有 ~22% 噪声，\n      可能导致修复方向偏移。这解释了为什么 re-repair lift 在 median 档只有 ~2.5%。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Diagnostic Signal Quality\"\n        columns: [Metric, Value]\n        rows:\n          - [Failure Precision, 0.78]\n          - [Failure Recall, 0.74]\n          - [Failure F1, 0.76]\n          - [Pass Precision, 0.88]\n          - [Pass Recall, 0.90]\n          - [False Positive Rate, 0.10]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Precision-Recall curve for failure class, 标注 operating point\"\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap: predicted vs actual pass/fail\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 Claim 2 的前提实验。78%/74% 的 precision/recall 表明 diagnostic signal 存在但有噪声。\n      足以作为 \"signal quality analysis\" 的正面结果，但不足以支撑 \"actionable diagnostics\" 的强叙事。\n      建议论文讨论 precision 阈值——在什么 precision 下 per-test info 开始帮助 vs 误导 repair agent。\n\n  - name: \"Diagnostic Re-Repair Pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"diagnostic-rerepair\"\n    description: >\n      200 实例上对比：repair agent 有 per-test failure 预测 vs 无 per-test 信息，比较 resolve rate。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_resolve_rate: 0.32\n      with_pertest_resolve_rate: 0.345\n      resolve_rate_lift_pct: 2.5\n      lift_absolute_instances: 5\n      p_value_mcnemar: 0.12\n      significant_at_005: false\n      significant_at_010: false\n      n_instances: 200\n      effect_size_cohens_h: 0.05\n      power_at_n200: 0.28\n    result_rationale: >\n      2.5% resolve rate lift（32% → 34.5%）在 n=200 下不显著（p=0.12）。\n      效应量极小（Cohen's h=0.05），统计检验功效只有 28%——需要 n≈2000 才能在 α=0.05 下\n      检测到这个 effect size。\n      lift 之所以小有三个原因：\n      (1) 69% 的实例只有 T=1 F2P 测试，per-test info 退化为 trajectory-level，无额外信息；\n      (2) 78% precision 意味着 ~22% 的 failure 预测是错误的，repair agent 有时被误导；\n      (3) 当前 repair agent（SWE-agent 级别）的 re-repair 能力有限，即使给出正确的 failure\n      定位，也不一定能修复。\n      这个结果在 median 档下是 \"suggestive but inconclusive\"——方向正确但证据不足。\n      论文应呈现为 pilot study，承认 underpowered，建议未来工作用更大样本验证。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Re-Repair Pilot Results\"\n        columns: [Condition, Resolve_Rate, N, \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [No per-test info, \"32.0%\", 200, \"[25.6%, 38.4%]\"]\n          - [With per-test predictions, \"34.5%\", 200, \"[27.9%, 41.1%]\"]\n          - [Lift, \"+2.5pp\", \"-\", \"p=0.12 (n.s.)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart with error bars: resolve rate ± 95% CI，两个条件\"\n      - \"Stratified lift by T: T=1 instances (lift ≈ 0%) vs T≥2 instances (lift ≈ 6-8%)\"\n    analysis: >\n      不显著的 re-repair lift 是 median 档对 Claim 2 的最大打击。论文策略：\n      (1) 将 per-test-precision-recall 作为 Claim 2 的主要证据（signal 存在）；\n      (2) re-repair 降级为 pilot/suggestive evidence；\n      (3) 展示 T≥2 子集的 stratified lift（预计 6-8%）作为 \"per-test info helps when it\n      provides new information\" 的支撑。\n\n  - name: \"Oracle F2P Stratified Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"oracle-f2p-stratified\"\n    description: >\n      按 F2P 测试数量 T=1, T=2, T=3+ 分层，报告 per-test vs trajectory 的 oracle advantage。\n    expected_results:\n      T1_pct_instances: 0.69\n      T1_iid_advantage: 0.02\n      T1_block_advantage: 0.05\n      T2_pct_instances: 0.19\n      T2_iid_advantage: 0.09\n      T2_block_advantage: 0.22\n      T3plus_pct_instances: 0.12\n      T3plus_iid_advantage: 0.18\n      T3plus_block_advantage: 0.38\n      population_weighted_iid_advantage: 0.046\n      population_weighted_block_advantage: 0.115\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 oracle 模拟的直接分解，结果由数学性质决定而非模型训练。\n      T=1 时 per-test 和 trajectory-level 在数学上几乎等价——唯一差异来自 per-test 模型\n      在该测试上的 calibration 可能不同于 trajectory 模型的整体 calibration。优势 ~2%。\n      T=2 时 per-test 可以区分\"两个测试都失败\"和\"只有一个测试失败\"的 patch，提供了\n      trajectory-level 无法获得的排序信号。i.i.d. 优势 ~9%，block-corr 下 ~22%。\n      T=3+ 时优势最大（i.i.d. 18%, block 38%），因为更多测试提供了更丰富的 ranking 信号。\n      但 T=3+ 只占 12% 的实例，所以 population-weighted advantage 被严重稀释。\n      Block correlation 在所有 T 下都放大优势，因为 correlated errors 降低了 effective\n      独立测试数，使每个测试的信息量更大。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Stratified Oracle Advantage\"\n        columns: [T_bucket, Pct_Instances, IID_Advantage, Block_Advantage]\n        rows:\n          - [\"T=1\", \"69%\", \"2.0%\", \"5.0%\"]\n          - [\"T=2\", \"19%\", \"9.0%\", \"22.0%\"]\n          - [\"T≥3\", \"12%\", \"18.0%\", \"38.0%\"]\n          - [\"Pop. Weighted\", \"100%\", \"4.6%\", \"11.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: per-T bucket advantage, i.i.d. vs block, 颜色区分\"\n      - \"Stacked area: SWE-bench T 分布直方图，叠加 per-test advantage 曲线\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 Claim 3 的核心表格，也是论文最强贡献。清晰展示 per-test advantage 集中在\n      T≥2 实例（31%），为 \"when to deploy per-test simulation\" 提供了 actionable decision rule。\n      建议论文标题或副标题直接引用这个发现。\n\n  - name: \"Block Correlation Empirical Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"block-corr-empirical\"\n    description: >\n      从训练好的 classification 模型的 test-level 预测中测量误差相关结构，\n      与 i.i.d. 和 block-corr 模拟对比。\n    expected_results:\n      empirical_spearman_vs_iid: 0.18\n      empirical_spearman_vs_block: 0.72\n      effective_rho: 0.22\n      ratio_to_block_model_rho: 0.44\n      iid_model_ks_test_p: 0.003\n      block_model_ks_test_p: 0.08\n    result_rationale: >\n      模型预测误差在同一 instance 内存在中等程度相关（Spearman vs i.i.d. = 0.18），\n      因为共享的代码上下文导致类似的 failure 模式（如模型对某种 assertion 风格系统性判错）。\n      但这种相关远低于 block model 假设的完全相关（Spearman vs block = 0.72）。\n      实际 effective rho ~0.22 大约是 block model rho 的 44%。\n      KS 检验显示 i.i.d. 模型被显著拒绝（p=0.003），block model 未被拒绝（p=0.08）\n      但也不算好的 fit。真实误差结构介于两者之间，更接近 i.i.d.。\n      这意味着 oracle 模拟中 block-corr 结果是上界估计，i.i.d. 结果更接近现实。\n      对论文叙事的影响：population-weighted advantage 的 realistic estimate 更接近\n      4.6%（i.i.d.）而非 11.5%（block），降低了 per-test 的整体优势主张。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Error Correlation Structure\"\n        columns: [Metric, Empirical, IID_Model, Block_Model]\n        rows:\n          - [Intra-instance error Spearman, 0.18, 0.0, 1.0]\n          - [Effective ρ, 0.22, 0.0, 0.50]\n          - [KS test p-value, \"-\", 0.003, 0.08]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: empirical error correlation matrix (test-pair) vs predicted under i.i.d. and block models\"\n    analysis: >\n      实证数据确认误差结构介于两个极端之间，effective T 更接近 i.i.d.。\n      这是论文诚实性的体现——block model 结果虽然好看，但不是最佳估计。\n      建议报告 calibrated advantage（插值 i.i.d. 和 block 结果）作为 point estimate。\n\n  - name: \"SWE-bench PerTest Data Construction\"\n    plan_id: \"swebench-pertest-data\"\n    description: >\n      Docker 重跑 SWE-bench Verified 的 patch，提取 per-test pass/fail 标签。\n      目标 500 instances × 16 candidates。\n    expected_results:\n      target_instances: 500\n      successful_instances: 420\n      failed_instances: 80\n      failure_rate: 0.16\n      failure_reasons:\n        docker_timeout: 35\n        env_setup_failure: 25\n        flaky_tests: 12\n        other: 8\n      total_candidate_test_pairs: 67200\n      avg_tests_per_instance: 42\n      avg_f2p_per_instance: 2.8\n      avg_p2p_per_instance: 39.2\n      compute_hours_wall: 22\n    result_rationale: >\n      16% 失败率反映 SWE-bench Docker 环境的现实复杂度。主要失败原因：\n      (1) Docker timeout（35 例）：部分 repo 的测试套件耗时超过容器限制，尤其是大型 Django/scipy 项目；\n      (2) 环境搭建失败（25 例）：依赖版本冲突、系统库缺失、Python 版本不匹配；\n      (3) Flaky tests（12 例）：测试结果在重跑间不一致，无法作为可靠标签。\n      420 个成功实例 × 16 candidates = 6720 instance-candidate pairs，每个平均 ~42 个测试，\n      总计 ~67k test-level labels。这个数据量足以支撑 repo-level 训练实验。\n      22h wall clock 在 16 并行容器下合理（~1.3h per instance 平均，考虑排队和重试）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Data statistics dashboard: instances per repo, T distribution histogram, failure mode breakdown\"\n    analysis: >\n      420 个实例（vs 目标 500）是可接受的 yield。更关键的是数据质量——需要验证 flaky test\n      过滤是否充分，以及 per-test labels 与官方 SWE-bench 的 trajectory-level labels 一致性。\n\n  - name: \"Repo-Level Training\"\n    plan_id: \"repo-level-training\"\n    description: >\n      在 SWE-bench-PerTest 数据上微调 Qwen3-4B/8B，预测 repo-level per-test pass/fail。\n    expected_results:\n      repo_4b_pass_f1: 0.72\n      repo_4b_fail_f1: 0.75\n      repo_4b_avg_f1: 0.735\n      repo_4b_accuracy: 0.74\n      repo_8b_pass_f1: 0.77\n      repo_8b_fail_f1: 0.79\n      repo_8b_avg_f1: 0.78\n      repo_8b_accuracy: 0.78\n      function_to_repo_drop_4b_pp: 14.0\n      function_to_repo_drop_8b_pp: 11.5\n      context_length_median_tokens: 4200\n      context_length_p95_tokens: 12800\n    result_rationale: >\n      Repo-level per-class F1 ~73.5% (4B) / ~78% (8B) 反映了 repo-level 任务的固有难度：\n      (1) 上下文长度大幅增加（中位 ~4200 tokens，P95 ~12800 tokens），超过 function-level 的\n      ~850 tokens 约 5 倍，4B 模型的注意力容量受限；\n      (2) 跨文件依赖要求模型理解 import 链、类继承、配置文件的影响，这在 function-level 不存在；\n      (3) 训练数据量更少（420 instances vs function-level 数千条），过拟合风险更高；\n      (4) 测试复杂度更高——repo-level 测试常涉及 fixture setup、database state、file I/O。\n      8B 模型比 4B 好 ~4.5pp，主要得益于更好的长上下文处理能力。\n      14pp drop（function → repo）对论文的影响：不能直接将 function-level 的结论泛化到 repo-level，\n      需要在论文中作为 separate evaluation 呈现，并诚实讨论 generalization gap。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Function-Level vs Repo-Level\"\n        columns: [Level, Model, Avg_F1, Accuracy]\n        rows:\n          - [Function, 4B, 0.875, 0.875]\n          - [Function, 8B, 0.895, 0.895]\n          - [Repo, 4B, 0.735, 0.740]\n          - [Repo, 8B, 0.780, 0.780]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar: function vs repo F1, 4B vs 8B, 误差条表示 per-repo 方差\"\n    analysis: >\n      Repo-level F1 在 median 档 [70-79] 范围内。结果 usable 但不 impressive。\n      论文策略：作为 \"preliminary extension\" 呈现，强调 function-level 是主要贡献，\n      repo-level 展示方法可行性但需要更多数据和更大模型。\n\n  - name: \"LLM-as-Judge Baselines\"\n    plan_id: \"llm-judge-baseline\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-8B/32B zero-shot LLM-as-judge，trajectory-level 和 per-test 两种模式。\n      作为 Pareto frontier 的参考点。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen3_8b_traj_accuracy: 0.65\n      qwen3_8b_pertest_accuracy: 0.62\n      qwen3_32b_traj_accuracy: 0.72\n      qwen3_32b_pertest_accuracy: 0.69\n      qwen3_8b_traj_f1: 0.63\n      qwen3_32b_traj_f1: 0.71\n      qwen3_8b_pertest_f1: 0.60\n      qwen3_32b_pertest_f1: 0.67\n      inference_cost_8b_per_instance_sec: 2.5\n      inference_cost_32b_per_instance_sec: 12.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Zero-shot LLM judge 缺乏 task-specific fine-tuning 信号，必须依赖通用代码理解能力。\n      8B zero-shot (~63% F1) 远低于 4B fine-tuned (~87.5%)，说明 fine-tuning 在这个任务上\n      价值巨大——通用代码理解不足以可靠预测执行结果。\n      32B 通过更强的代码推理能力达到 ~71% F1，但仍低于 fine-tuned 4B。\n      Per-test 模式比 trajectory 略差 2-3pp，因为 per-test 需要更精细的推理（判断单个测试的\n      具体行为），而 trajectory-level 可以利用更多启发式规则（如\"代码改动小 → 大概率 pass\"）。\n      这些 baseline 在 Pareto frontier 上提供了 \"high cost, moderate accuracy\" 的参考点，\n      与 fine-tuned classification 的 \"low cost, high accuracy\" 形成清晰对比。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: Pareto Frontier Reference Points\"\n        columns: [Model, Mode, Params, Fine-tuned, F1, Cost_per_instance]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-4B LoRA, Per-test Classification, 4B, Yes, 0.875, \"0.3s\"]\n          - [Qwen3-4B LoRA, CWM Generation, 4B, Yes, 0.795, \"0.8s\"]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, \"Zero-shot Traj\", 8B, No, 0.63, \"2.5s\"]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, \"Zero-shot Per-test\", 8B, No, 0.60, \"2.5s\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, \"Zero-shot Traj\", 32B, No, 0.71, \"12s\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, \"Zero-shot Per-test\", 32B, No, 0.67, \"12s\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Pareto frontier scatter: x=cost (inference time), y=F1, 每个方法一个点，Pareto 前沿线\"\n    analysis: >\n      Fine-tuned 4B classification 在 Pareto frontier 上占据最优位置——最低成本且最高精度。\n      这个结果强化了 Claim 1 的实用性论点：不仅 formulation 更好，还更高效。\n      32B zero-shot 接近但未超过 4B fine-tuned CWM，有趣但不意外。\n\n  - name: \"Per-Test Majority Voting (K=3)\"\n    plan_id: \"per-test-majority-voting\"\n    description: >\n      Classification 模型 K=3 self-consistency，测试多数投票是否提升 per-test 精度。\n    expected_results:\n      single_pass_f1: 0.875\n      majority_k3_f1: 0.885\n      improvement_pp: 1.0\n      compute_multiplier: 3.0\n      marginal_gain_per_compute: 0.33\n      agreement_rate_k3: 0.92\n      flip_rate_correct_to_wrong: 0.02\n      flip_rate_wrong_to_correct: 0.04\n    result_rationale: >\n      Majority voting 带来 ~1pp 改进（87.5% → 88.5%），因为 classification 任务已经在\n      单次推理下达到较高 calibration。92% 的样本三次预测完全一致，意味着大部分 uncertainty\n      已经在单次推理中被解决。\n      剩余 8% 不一致的样本中，4% 从错误翻转为正确（2:1 多数），2% 从正确翻转为错误（1:2 少数）。\n      净增益 = 4% - 2% = 2%，但由于只影响 8% 的样本，总体改进 ≈ 2% × 8% / (scale) ≈ 1pp。\n      3 倍推理成本换取 1pp 改进，成本效益比低。论文可以在 appendix 中报告但不作为主要结果。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A1 (Appendix): Self-Consistency\"\n        columns: [K, F1, Compute, Marginal_Gain_per_Compute]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.875, \"1×\", \"-\"]\n          - [3, 0.885, \"3×\", \"0.33pp/×\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      边际收益递减，确认 classification formulation 已经达到该模型规模下的近最优预测。\n      这间接支撑了 Claim 1——classification 不需要额外 test-time compute tricks 就能达到高精度。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5e2ff9bf-0df6-4a54-a6c1-9e43e44e7de7","total_cost_usd":0.687172,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35970,"cache_read_input_tokens":206699,"output_tokens":14157,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35970,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":13177,"cache_read_input_tokens":45680,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2131},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4935,"outputTokens":22,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.005045,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":14157,"cacheReadInputTokens":206699,"cacheCreationInputTokens":35970,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6821269999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"bbb8df5f-a49b-4b52-9c40-2d41169acd9d"}
